From: Cosmopod OS Build Team <builds@cosmopod.invalid>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 23:25:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] debuginfod: keep strchr result const

The HTTP header input is const and the matching colon is never modified.
Keep the const qualifier required by newer glibc headers.

Upstream-Status: Pending

---
 debuginfod/debuginfod-client.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/debuginfod/debuginfod-client.c b/debuginfod/debuginfod-client.c
index 6b8a99a..c3c54f6 100644
--- a/debuginfod/debuginfod-client.c
+++ b/debuginfod/debuginfod-client.c
@@ -2031,7 +2031,7 @@ int debuginfod_add_http_header (debuginfod_client *client, const char* header)
   /* Sanity check header value is of the form Header: Value.
      It should contain at least one colon that isn't the first or
      last character.  */
-  char *colon = strchr (header, ':'); /* first colon */
+  const char *colon = strchr (header, ':'); /* first colon */
   if (colon == NULL /* present */
       || colon == header /* not at beginning - i.e., have a header name */
       || *(colon + 1) == '\0') /* not at end - i.e., have a value */
-- 
2.43.0
